still doesn't make sense.

511
00:24:52,180 --> 00:24:54,137
Vander Decken must be quite ancient.

512
00:24:54,220 --> 00:24:57,417
If he isn't a ghost, I imagine
he's a few hundred years old.

513
00:24:57,500 --> 00:24:58,330
At least.

514
00:24:58,800 --> 00:24:59,630
Huh.

515
00:24:59,780 --> 00:25:01,837
You're right, that doesn't make sense.

516
00:25:01,920 --> 00:25:04,380
That is, unless you ignore the rumors.

517
00:25:04,860 --> 00:25:07,213
Now, there's no denying that he existed.

518
00:25:07,320 --> 00:25:09,837
But the truth of the matter is
that the legendary sea captain

519
00:25:09,920 --> 00:25:13,757
Vander Decken died sometime after
he arrived here on Fishman Island?

520
00:25:13,840 --> 00:25:15,781
and hasn't been heard from since.

521
00:25:16,420 --> 00:25:21,720
That said, the ship you say you saw
probably was the Flying Dutchman, but...

522
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:24,939
It's his descendant who's on board.

523
00:25:26,920 --> 00:25:27,750
He's...

524
00:25:27,833 --> 00:25:29,066
He's Vander Decken the Ninth.

525
00:25:31,720 --> 00:25:33,200
Wow, that's a lot!

526
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:37,537
Well, I have to say, it's a relief to
find out he's not a ghost after all.

527
00:25:37,620 --> 00:25:39,537
Believing we had come into
contact with someone from

528
00:25:39,620 --> 00:25:42,637
the afterlife was making me
contemplate my own mortality.

529
00:25:42,720 --> 00:25:45,557
And considering I'm a skeleton,
I don't have much of that left.

530
00:25:45,640 --> 00:25:48,380
I just wanted to tell an exciting story.

531
00:25:49,500 --> 00:25:52,377
Man, I thought merfolk and
fishmen all look the same,

532
00:25:52,460 --> 00:25:54,177
but the more I see, the less they do.

533
00:25:54,260 --> 00:25:55,917
Check out those old ones down there.

534
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:58,217
Their fins are split like Granny Kokoro.

535
00:25:58,300 --> 00:26:00,080
See those babies? Right there.

536
00:26:01,280 --> 00:26:05,697
You'll notice the father is a fishman, but
the children are a mix of both species.

537
00:26:05,780 --> 00:26:07,737
That's because when a
mermaid and a fishman

538
00:26:07,820 --> 00:26:10,277
love each other very much
and decide to get busy,

539
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:13,360
Their kids can come out
looking like either parent.

540
00:26:13,460 --> 00:26:14,290
Bam!

541
00:26:14,373 --> 00:26:16,693
Four possibilities for the happy family.

542
00:26:16,840 --> 00:26:19,252
Whoa, that's why they all look different.

543
00:26:19,420 --> 00:26:20,340
So cool.

544
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:23,847
All right, we finally
made it to the highway.

545
00:26:27,300 --> 00:26:28,130
Whoa!

546
00:26:28,240 --> 00:26:29,420
This is fast!

547
00:26:30,480 --> 00:26:31,917
What's up with that place?

548
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:32,920
Oh, nothing.

549
00:26:33,020 --> 00:26:34,237
It's a candy factory.

550
00:26:34,320 --> 00:26:35,150
Really?

551
00:26:35,233 --> 00:26:36,937
Then why is there a pirate flag on it?

552
00:26:37,020 --> 00:26:37,850
Oh, that?

553
00:26:37,933 --> 00:26:39,057
That flag's everywhere here.

554
00:26:39,140 --> 00:26:41,917
By the entrance and the
harbor, it's a big deal.

555
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:46,660
And for good reason at that, it
symbolizes that we're protected. You see,

556
00:26:46,880 --> 00:26:51,117
the flag belongs to a famous pirate
named Charlotte Lin-Lin of the New World.

557
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:54,729
But she's better known as Big
Mom, one of the four emperors.

558
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:56,640
Whoa, that's no joke.

559
00:26:57,420 --> 00:27:01,097
Back before the war in Marineford,
Whitebeard was this island's guardian.

560
00:27:01,180 --> 00:27:03,697
But now that he's dead, someone
else had to take his place.

561
00:27:03,780 --> 00:27:05,898
And that someone happened to be her.

562
00:27:06,500 --> 00:27:07,330
Okay.

563
00:27:07,840 --> 00:27:12,311
The thing is, she demands a whole ton
of candy in exchange for her services.

564
00:27:12,760 --> 00:27:14,878
Hence the factory that you just saw.

565
00:27:15,120 --> 00:27:15,950
That's weird.

566
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:18,477
This country wouldn't be
able to survive without

567
00:27:18,560 --> 00:27:20,737
the protection of
powerful people like her.

568
00:27:20,820 --> 00:27:23,497
After all, this is a dangerous
place where pirates come and go,

569
00:27:23,580 --> 00:27:26,197
and more often than not,
they aren't very friendly.

570
00:27:26,280 --> 00:27:27,110
Yeah, I guess.

571
00:27:27,260 --> 00:27:29,577
Plus, she's filling in
where Whitebeard left off,

572
00:27:29,660 --> 00:27:32,097
so that's gotta mean she's
a good person, doesn't it?

573
00:27:32,180 --> 00:27:33,757
Depends on how you look at it.

574
00:27:33,840 --> 00:27:36,857
Whitebeard never asked for anything
in return for his protection.

575
00:27:36,940 --> 00:27:40,337
Big Mom, on the other hand, treats it
like a business rather than a charity.

576
00:27:40,420 --> 00:27:41,560
Still, that's cool.

577
00:27:41,860 --> 00:27:44,860
An emperor. Like shakes. Crazy.

578
00:27:45,140 --> 00:27:46,669
Hope they get to meet her.

579
00:27:46,820 --> 00:27:47,650
Eyes forward.

580
00:27:48,120 --> 00:27:50,649
This is where all the
celebrity types live.

581
00:27:50,760 --> 00:27:51,800
Fishburly Hills.

582
00:27:53,340 --> 00:27:57,577
That tall building right in front is
Papa Goose's house, where we're going.

583
00:27:57,660 --> 00:27:58,490
All that?

584
00:27:58,780 --> 00:28:00,420
For one starfish?

585
00:28:03,240 --> 00:28:04,070
Ah!

586
00:28:06,940 --> 00:28:08,257
We have to do something.

587
00:28:08,340 --> 00:28:10,080
We can't let this happen.

588
00:28:10,440 --> 00:28:12,720
That's Madame Shirley, from the cafe.

589
00:28:13,280 --> 00:28:14,339
What's the matter?

590
00:28:14,460 --> 00:28:15,840
Please, please tell us.

591
00:28:16,140 --> 00:28:16,970
What's wrong?

592
00:28:17,053 --> 00:28:17,883
Why are you upset?

593
00:28:17,980 --> 00:28:19,380
Something must be done.

594
00:28:19,540 --> 00:28:21,011
Now before it's too late.

595
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:22,470
Sure.

596
00:28:22,553 --> 00:28:23,383
What do we do?

597
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:26,600
Find him!

598
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:29,020
The pirate boy in a Straw Hat!

599
00:28:29,120 --> 00:28:30,179
It's an emergency!

600
00:28:32,060 --> 00:28:34,420
He must leave the country! Now!

601
00:28:34,660 --> 00:28:35,537
There's no time!

602
00:28:35,620 --> 00:28:37,700
Wait, you're having a premonition?

603
00:28:37,960 --> 00:28:42,607
I swore I wouldn't use this power, but
something about that boy felt off to me.

604
00:28:42,940 --> 00:28:43,770
I...

605
00:28:43,853 --> 00:28:46,220
I had no choice but to
look into the future.

606
00:28:47,940 --> 00:28:49,293
What's going to happen?

607
00:28:49,620 --> 00:28:51,149
Tell us, what did you see?

608
00:28:51,340 --> 00:28:52,520
We have to know!

609
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:55,080
Charlie, tell us!

610
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:56,780
Madam, please!

611
00:28:58,180 --> 00:29:01,700
I hope I'm wrong, and
that it won't happen.

612
00:29:08,460 --> 00:29:10,340
I saw him clearly,

613
00:29:10,620 --> 00:29:11,960
surrounded by flames,

614
00:29:12,200 --> 00:29:17,097
because Straw Hat Luffy, Fishman Island,

615
00:29:17,180 --> 00:29:20,180
our country will be destroyed.
